  "analysis": {
    "kind": "bug-fix",
    "originalLogic": "`can_simplify` scans the switchInt targets and requires all targets have identical destinations and equal statement-list lengths. For each corresponding statement pair it classifies: identical statements, equal constants (`SameByEq`), or constants that might be reachable by extending/truncating the case value (`CompareType::Discr { is_signed }`). It then validates all remaining targets against this pattern and, in `new_stmts`, replaces the arms with `discr as target_ty (IntToInt)`. The old classification used `int_equal(l,r,size) = l.to_bits_unchecked() == ScalarInt::try_from_uint(r,size).unwrap().to_bits_unchecked()` plus an `is_signed` flag derived from `f_c.const_.ty().is_signed() || discr_ty.is_signed()`.",
    "incorrectTransformation": "The historical `CompareType::Discr` rewrite could replace a multi-arm match with `discr as T (IntToInt)` even when the arm constant was NOT the result of IntToInt on the case value, because its signed/unsigned test mixed zext and sext semantics. Concretely, for `#[repr(i8)] enum` value `-1i8` (bit pattern 0xFF) with arm `=> 255i16`, the old logic accepted the bit equality and emitted `discr as i16`, whose sign extension gives `-1i16` (0xFFFF), not `255i16` (0x00FF). This is the unsound direction: bit-pattern equality at the source size was treated as cast equality at the target size. The same error applied to `-1i8 => 255u16`, and analogous truncation cases.",
    "inputDomain": "Exhaustively-covered integer enums (or integer switchInt discriminants) whose arms return integer constants, with cross-width and/or cross-signedness relations, e.g. i8/u8 -> i8/u8, i8 -> i16/u16, u8 -> i16/u16, i16/u16 -> i8/u8, and same-width i128/u128. Both successful folds and \"failed\" cases where the arm constant is deliberately not the IntToInt result (wildcard/fallback arms and differing arm statement lengths are separate non-trigger conditions).",
    "passIds": [
      "MatchBranchSimplification"
    ],
    "summary": "MatchBranchSimplification folds an integer-discriminant switchInt into a single `discriminant as T (IntToInt)` when every arm yields a constant obtainable by that cast. This PR fixes the prior unsound heuristic (#124150): the old CompareType::Discr logic mixed sign/zero extension and could rewrite `-1i8` matched to `255i16` as `discr as i16`, which actually yields `-1`. The fix replaces the flag-based comparison with a `can_cast` helper that computes the real IntToInt result (sext for i8->i16/u16, zext for u8->i16/u16, trunc for i16/u16->i8/u8) and requires it to equal the target ScalarInt before enabling the transform, then removes the unsound_mir_opts gate.",
    "trigger": "`MatchBranchSimplification` sees a `switchInt` on an integer discriminant where all targets lead to identical statement structures assigning constants, and each discriminant case value cast via `IntToInt` to the target constant type equals that arm's constant. When a case value is negative/narrow or a wide value truncates, the actual IntToInt semantics determine whether the transform is valid.",
    "preconditions": [
      "Discriminant type is an integer (`Uint` or `Int`) and arm constants are integer scalars.",
      "All switchInt targets have identical destination places and same-length statement lists; each relevant statement is an assignment of a constant to the same place.",
      "Every case value must satisfy `can_cast`: convert the case value to its signed/unsigned interpretation per `src_layout.ty` (Uint => to_uint, Int => to_int as u128), truncate to the target integer type's size, build a ScalarInt, and compare equal to the arm's target ScalarInt.",
      "For i8->i16/u16 the result must reflect sign extension; for u8->i16/u16 zero extension; for i16/u16->i8/u8 truncation.",
      "The transform must only be applied once the can_cast equality holds for the first/second arms and every remaining target."
    ],
    "pitfalls": [
      "Do not decide cast compatibility from `is_signed` flags or raw `to_bits_unchecked()` equality at the source size; compare the actual IntToInt result at the target size.",
      "Sign extension: i8 -1 -> i16 is -1 (0xFFFF), not 255 (0x00FF); u8 255 -> i16 is 255.",
      "i8 -> u16 sign-extends then reinterprets: -1i8 -> 0xFFFF (65535), -128i8 -> 0xFF80 (65408); it is not zero extension.",
      "Truncation: i16 -127 -> i8 = -127 (0x81), so an arm of 127i8 must block the fold; u16 65535 -> u8 = 255, so 127u8 must block; u16 65535 -> i8 = -1.",
      "Same-width i128->u128 does not numerically convert; the discriminant bit pattern is preserved, so an exhaustive i128 enum can fold to `discr as u128`.",
      "The old buggy transform was gated behind `unsound_mir_opts`; simply removing that gate without replacing the comparison would expose the miscompile.",
      "Do not conflate this with fallback/wildcard arms or arm-length mismatches, which independently prevent the simplification."
    ],
    "testStrategy": "Add MIR-opt tests under `tests/mir-opt/matches_reduce_branches.rs` with `// EMIT_MIR` and per-case `.MatchBranchSimplification.diff` expectations. Use exhaustive `#[repr(u8/i8/u16/i16)]` enums whose variant names encode signedness and radix (e.g. `_1_0xff`, `u255_0xff`) so each cast class is unambiguous. Provide positive cases asserting `// CHECK-NOT: switchInt` and `// CHECK: IntToInt` / `// CHECK: return`, and paired `*_failed` cases with one arm constant changed to the wrong sext/zext/trunc result asserting `// CHECK: switchInt`. Cover every bucket: no-op (u8->i8, u8->u8), sext (i8->i16, i8->u16), zext (u8->i16, u8->u16), trunc (i16/u16->i8/u8), same-width i128->u128, multi-statement arms (`.u8_i8_2`), fallback arms, and different arm statement lengths (custom_mir `*_failed_len_*`). This lets a separate agent build two programs differing only in the constant/transform and observe fold vs no-fold.",
    "evidence": [
      "The condition in #120614 is wrong, e.g. `-1i8` cannot be converted to `255i16`.",
      "The new approach is to check **if the case value after the `IntToInt` conversion equals the target value**.",
      "- `i8` to `i16`/`u16`: sign extension.",
      "- `u8` to `i16`/`u16`: zero extension.",
      "- `i16`/`u16` to `i8`/`u8`: truncate to the target size.",
      "The previous error was a mix of zext and sext.",
      "// unsound: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/124150",
      "l.to_bits_unchecked() == ScalarInt::try_from_uint(r, size).unwrap().to_bits_unchecked()",
      "&& s_c.const_.ty().is_signed()",
      "let v = size.truncate(v);",
      "cast_scalar == target_scalar",
      "/// Check if the cast constant using `IntToInt` is equal to the target constant.",
      "// Converting `-1i8` to `255i16` is zext.",
      "// Converting `-1i8` to `255u16` is zext.",
      "EnumAi8::_1_0xff => 255, // failed",
      "EnumAu16::u65535_0xffff => 127, // failed",
      "EnumAi16::o127_0xff7f => -127, // failed",
      "// CHECK-NOT: switchInt",
      "// CHECK: IntToInt"
    ],
